    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "I want to disable mini.pairs for markdown files because it gets in the way of writing code blocks with triple ` . I wrote this: \r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"FileType\", {\r\n  pattern = { \"gitcommit\", \"markdown\" },\r\n  callback = function()\r\n    vim.b.mini_pairs_disable = true\r\n  end,\r\n})\r\n```\r\nBut it gives the warning `Fields cannot be injected into the reference of `table<number, table<string, any>>` for `mini_pairs_disable`. To allow injection, add `[any]: any` to the definition.`\r\n\r\nHow do I fix this? Would it be easier to just unmap ` in that buffer because I like using everything else about the plugin?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I want to disable mini.pairs for markdown files because it gets in the way of writing code blocks with triple ` . I wrote this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(&quot;FileType&quot;, {\n  pattern = { &quot;gitcommit&quot;, &quot;markdown&quot; },\n  callback = function()\n    vim.b.mini_pairs_disable = true\n  end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>FileType<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, {\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">pattern</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> { <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>gitcommit<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>markdown<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>},\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">mini_pairs_disable</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But it gives the warning <code class=\"notranslate\">Fields cannot be injected into the reference of </code>table&lt;number, table&lt;string, any&gt;&gt;<code class=\"notranslate\">for</code>mini_pairs_disable<code class=\"notranslate\">. To allow injection, add </code>[any]: any<code class=\"notranslate\"> to the definition.</code></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How do I fix this? Would it be easier to just unmap ` in that buffer because I like using everything else about the plugin?</p>",
    "bodyText": "I want to disable mini.pairs for markdown files because it gets in the way of writing code blocks with triple ` . I wrote this:\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"FileType\", {\n  pattern = { \"gitcommit\", \"markdown\" },\n  callback = function()\n    vim.b.mini_pairs_disable = true\n  end,\n})\nBut it gives the warning Fields cannot be injected into the reference of table<number, table<string, any>>formini_pairs_disable. To allow injection, add [any]: any to the definition.\nHow do I fix this? Would it be easier to just unmap ` in that buffer because I like using everything else about the plugin?",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
